-/// "Обход одноразовых" / "Обход с таймером" — the part that makes them real.
-///
-/// The display half (`ChatMessageInteractiveMediaNode`) only stops drawing a self-destructing
-/// photo/video blurred. Telegram still treats the message as secret everywhere else: a tap opens
-/// `SecretMediaPreviewController`, which starts the countdown (and reports the content as opened),
-/// the picture is capture-protected, and save/copy/forward are hidden — so the photo vanished when
-/// the timer ran out and could never be saved.
-///
-/// This removes the self-destruct timers from the *local copy* of the message: the
-/// `AutoremoveTimeoutMessageAttribute` / `AutoclearTimeoutMessageAttribute` that
-/// `Message.containsSecretMedia` is derived from. From then on the message is an ordinary photo or
-/// video for every screen — regular gallery, regular context menu, "Сохранить" — and nothing ever
-/// starts a countdown or sends `readMessageContents`, so the original stays where it is and the
-/// sender never sees it opened. Nothing is sent to Telegram.
-///
-/// Scope, on purpose: incoming photos, videos and GIFs in cloud chats only, and only while the
-/// toggle matching the message's kind is on. Secret chats are never touched (see the footer of the
-/// "Медиа и скриншоты" block), and neither are voice / music / round videos, which have their own
-/// players and their own "listened" bookkeeping.
-///
-/// Lives here rather than in a separate mod module for the same reason `PampGramSecretMediaPrefetch`
-/// does: it needs `TelegramCore`-only types, and `PampGramCore` must never depend back on them.
